<title>UK: GOLF-WOODS PLAYS WITH ELKINGTON, LANGER AT OPEN.</title>
<headline>GOLF-WOODS PLAYS WITH ELKINGTON, LANGER AT OPEN.</headline>
<dateline>TROON, Scotland 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>World number one Tiger</p>
<p>Woods was drawn on Tuesday to play with Players Championship</p>
<p>winner Steve Elkington of Australia and German Bernhard Langer</p>
<p>in the first two rounds of the British Open starting a Royal</p>
<p>Troon on Thursday.</p>
<p>The three players have won an aggregate nine tournaments</p>
<p>this year.</p>
<p>Woods has captured the Masters,  three other U.S. Tour events</p>
<p>and the Asian Classic, Elkington has won the Doral Open as well</p>
<p>as the Players Championhip and Langer won the Italian and Benson</p>
<p>and Hedges International Opens on the European Tour in</p>
<p>successive weeks.</p>
<p>Woods, 21, and his partners will tee off at 1205 GMT on</p>
<p>Thursday and then will have an early start at 0745 on Friday.</p>
<p>Defending champion Tom Lehman will be two groups behind</p>
<p>fellow American Woods for the opening two rounds, playing with</p>
<p>Vijay Singh of Fiji and Spaniard Miguel Martin at 1225 and 0805</p>
<p>on Thursday and Friday.</p>
<p>Three groups further back will be three-times champion Nick</p>
<p>Faldo of Britain with 1994 winner Nick Price of Zimbabwe and</p>
<p>American Tommy Tolles.</p>
<p>The first big-name group on opening day will comprise U.S.</p>
<p>Open runner-up Colin Montgomerie of Britain, five-times champion</p>
<p>Tom Watson of the U.S. and Mark McNulty of Zimbabwe.</p>
<p>They begin at 0735 on Thursday and resume at 1155 on Friday.</p>
<p>U.S. Open champion Ernie Els plays with twice U.S. Open</p>
<p>winner Curtis Strange and Jonathan Lomas of Britain at 1105 on</p>
<p>the opening day.</p>
